# ==============================================================================
# Vela — Voice Banking on a Routed Vendor Stack
# ==============================================================================
# Copy this file to `.env` and fill in what you have:
#
#     make env      creates .env from this file
#     make verify   prints each chain and says which links your keys can reach
#
# Only the first two are required. The voice chain is a chain on purpose — the
# router skips providers whose credentials are absent, so the agent runs on
# whichever keys you hold. With just DEEPGRAM_API_KEY it speaks and listens
# through Deepgram alone; every key you add is one more thing that can fail
# without the caller hearing it.
#
# NEVER commit `.env` — it is gitignored on purpose.
# ==============================================================================

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Required — Rasa Pro
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Free Developer Edition license (a long JWT, all on one line, no quotes).
# Request one: https://rasa.com/rasa-pro-developer-edition-license-key-request/
RASA_LICENSE=

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Required — LLM (routing + conversation)
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Also the third link in the TTS chain (gpt-4o-mini-tts), so this one key buys
# both the orchestrator and a last hosted voice.
# https://platform.openai.com/api-keys
OPENAI_API_KEY=

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The voice chain — bring what you have
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# First in the ASR chain, second in the TTS chain. The one key that gets you a
# working agent on its own. https://console.deepgram.com/
DEEPGRAM_API_KEY=

# Vela's own voice, and the first link in the TTS chain. Without it she still
# speaks — in Deepgram's voice, from the first word rather than after a failure.
# https://rime.ai/
RIME_API_KEY=

# Second in the ASR chain. A different company on different infrastructure,
# which is the only kind of fallback worth having. https://www.speechmatics.com/
SPEECHMATICS_API_KEY=

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Optional — development
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# LOG_LEVEL=INFO
# RASA_TELEMETRY_ENABLED=false
